# JARVIS PLATFORM — SECRETS
# Copy to: /opt/jarvis/config/secrets.env
# chmod 600 /opt/jarvis/config/secrets.env
# Never commit the real secrets.env file

# Slack (get from api.slack.com/apps)
# NOTE: comments go on their own line, never after a value. systemd's
# EnvironmentFile does NOT strip a trailing "# ..." — it becomes part of the
# value. These two lines used to carry inline comments, in the same file that
# warns about exactly that hazard for the guardrails three sections below.
# Bot User OAuth Token:
SLACK_BOT_TOKEN=xoxb-YOUR-TOKEN-HERE
# App-Level Token, for Socket Mode:
SLACK_APP_TOKEN=xapp-YOUR-APP-TOKEN-HERE
# To generate SLACK_APP_TOKEN:
#   1. api.slack.com/apps → Your App → Socket Mode → Enable
#   2. App-Level Tokens → Generate Token → name it "jarvis-socket" → scope: connections:write
#   3. Copy the xapp-... value here, then: systemctl restart jarvis-slack
JARVIS_SLACK_CHANNEL=#jarvis

# Anthropic Messages API key (metered, NOT the claude.ai subscription login
# used by spawn-agent.js workers / the primary brain — see CLAUDE.md's "THE
# ELEVEN SERVICES" note on brain-claude.js). Optional/fallback-only, THREE uses:
#   1. slack-bridge.js's Haiku intent classifier — ~300ms instead of the
#      3-10s claude-CLI cold start (falls back to the CLI without this key).
#   2. lib/agent.js's 'anthropic' provider — an emergency fallback brain if
#      the subscription session (provider 'claude') is unavailable.
#   3. lib/conversation.js's classifyIntent() Haiku fast-path — same ~300ms
#      win as #1, but for the Gateway/voice brain's own (separate) intent
#      classifier. Falls back to its own CLI path automatically without this.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-YOUR-KEY-HERE

# Notification tuning (all optional — defaults shown).
# Comments live on their OWN lines here, always — systemd's EnvironmentFile
# does NOT strip inline "# ..." comments off a value, so "30  # some note"
# is parsed as the literal string "30  # some note", not the number 30. That
# exact bug (guardrail values silently turning into NaN/unparseable strings)
# caused a real runaway-dispatch incident on 2026-07-17 (see self-heal.js's
# guardrail() and slack-bridge.js's guardedNumber()) — don't reintroduce it
# by adding a same-line comment back to any of these.
JARVIS_DIGEST_MINUTES=30
JARVIS_NOTIFY_COOLDOWN_MINUTES=30
JARVIS_MAX_IMMEDIATE_PER_HOUR=15
JARVIS_QUIET_HOURS=22-7

# This machine's own IP, as it appears in config/platforms.json's "server"
# field — lets orchestrator.js tell local vs remote platforms apart.
# Set this per-machine (primary vs standby use different values).
OWN_IP=66.42.121.161

# Chromium binary (auto-detected by install.sh)
CHROMIUM_BIN=chromium-browser

# Platform repo paths on this server
ZOOBICON_PATH=/var/www/zoobicon
ALECRAE_PATH=/var/www/alecrae
GATETEST_PATH=/var/www/gatetest
# VAPRON_PATH removed 2026-07-23 — Vapron has never had a local checkout on
# this box (it lives on box 158, config/platforms.json's vapron.server);
# audit-runner.js now audits it URL-only instead of trying to build it here.

# Gateway (docs/GATEWAY.md)
JARVIS_GATEWAY_TOKEN=
NOTIFY_SLACK_LEGACY=1

# ── PC mutation confirmation secret (src/lib/pc-confirm.js, 2026-08-19) ──────
# Shared HMAC secret that lets the deck/gateway PROVE to the orchestrator that a
# human confirmed a MUTATING PC action (shell / service.restart / process.kill).
# Held by deck, gateway and orchestrator (all load this file); STRIPPED from
# every spawned agent's env (claude-auth.js profileEnv), so a prompt-injected
# fleet agent cannot forge a confirmation and drive Craig's PC. Unset = the
# orchestrator fails CLOSED on mutations (read-only PC verbs still work).
# Generate: openssl rand -hex 32
JARVIS_PC_CONFIRM_SECRET=

# ── Deck: Tailscale identity login (src/lib/tailnet-identity.js, 2026-08-19) ─
# Comma-separated tailnet logins that unlock the Command Deck WITHOUT the deck
# token, when the request arrives through `tailscale serve` (the proxy injects
# Tailscale-User-Login from whois and strips client copies). This is what lets a
# PHONE in: the deck had refused Craig's iPhone ten times — logged with his own
# tailnet identity on the line — because the only credential was a token in a
# file on the box. Tagged nodes (fleet boxes, the PC) carry no login and keep
# using the token/cookie. Unset = off. Not a secret, but lives here because the
# deck unit's only EnvironmentFile is this one.
DECK_TAILNET_USERS=

# ── Device push (src/lib/push.js, docs/ALERTS.md) ────────────────────────────
# The alert path that works when NOTHING of Craig's is open — every other path
# (inbox, gateway push, deck push, TTS) needs a live tab or a poll.
# The TOPIC NAME IS THE CREDENTIAL: anyone who knows it can read and post to it,
# so keep it long and random and never commit it. Generate one with:
#   echo "jarvis-$(openssl rand -hex 12)"
# Then install the ntfy app (iOS/Android/desktop/web) on each device and
# subscribe to that topic. Unset = device alerts are OFF (logged once, at boot).
NTFY_TOPIC=
# Self-hosted ntfy instead of the public relay (optional).
NTFY_SERVER=https://ntfy.sh
# Bearer token, only needed for a reserved topic or a private server.
NTFY_TOKEN=
# Lowest level that reaches a device: info | warn | alert. Default warn —
# a phone that buzzes for routine chatter gets muted, and a muted channel is
# worse than no channel (see notify-center.js and the Slack firehose).
PUSH_MIN_LEVEL=warn
# Where tapping the notification takes him (the deck, over the tailnet).
PUSH_CLICK_URL=https://jarvis.tailbd6217.ts.net:8444/
# Guardrails — both go through lib/guardrail.js, so an inline comment here
# cannot silently disable them.
PUSH_MAX_PER_HOUR=12
PUSH_DEDUPE_MINUTES=10
# How long an IDENTICAL alert headline waits before it can buzz again. Alerts are
# exempt from the hourly cap (a storm of distinct criticals is signal) but not from
# this: an agent that re-runs on cron re-escalates anything still unfixed, so the
# same alert would otherwise arrive every run for as long as the problem lasts.
PUSH_ALERT_DEDUPE_HOURS=6
# Kill switch: 1 = no device push at all.
PUSH_DISABLED=

# ── Who may command Jarvis from Slack (src/lib/slack-auth.js) ────────────────
# Comma-separated Slack USER ids (not names): SLACK_ALLOWED_USERS=U01ABC123,U04XYZ
# FAILS CLOSED — with this unset, no Slack message is acted on at all. That is
# deliberate: unlike the deck and the gateway, the Slack dispatch path has NO
# confirmation turn (handleDispatch POSTs straight to /dispatch), so one message
# from anyone in the workspace was one full-permission root agent. Until
# 2026-07-30 there was no sender check at all.
# Don't know your id? Send the bot any message — the refusal is announced to the
# inbox WITH the id, once per unknown sender, so you can copy it from there.
SLACK_ALLOWED_USERS=
